  "question": {
    "text": "The equivalent conductance of NaCl at concentration C and at infinite dilution are <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mtext>C</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mo>∞</mo> </msub> </mrow> </math>, respectively. The correct relationship between <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mtext>C</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>λ</mi> <mo>∞</mo> </msub> </mrow> </math> is given as :<br />\r(where the constant B is positive)",
